OL,3,GNEWSAMLAs to debate bill aimed at
OL,4,Abanning conversion practices
OL,5,
OL,6,FA bill aimed at banning sexuality and
OL,7,Fgender conversion practices will be
OL,8,Fdebated by assembly members (MLAs) for
OL,9,Fthe first time at Stormont later on
OL,10,FTuesday.
OL,12,FIt contains provisions that could see a
OL,13,Ftwo-year jail sentence imposed on
OL,14,Fpeople who conduct conversion
OL,15,Fpractices.
OL,17,FAlliance's deputy leader Eoin Tennyson
OL,18,Fproposed the private member's
OL,19,Flegislation, but it has been criticised
OL,20,Fby the Democratic Unionist Party (DUP)
OL,21,Fwhich said the bill "presents a real
OL,22,Fthreat to freedom".
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
